WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:04.420
51. Wired for love?

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:13.210
In 2016, newspapers reported that a French woman had said something very strange.

3
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:20.210
She was engaged to a robot and planned to marry it as soon as robot human marriage became legal.

4
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:27.210
A strange story, yes. But in fact, people falling in love with non-human objects is nothing new.

5
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:33.210
People have married the Eiffel Tower, the Berlin Wall, and even the Statue of Liberty.

6
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:39.210
In the past, these affairs were seen as strange, and the people involved in them rather odd.

7
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:47.210
Technology is now so advanced, however, that certain objects, such as computers and robots, can seem almost human.

8
00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:56.210
The question is no longer a joke. Could there be a future in which human-robot relationships not only exist, but are considered normal?

9
00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:03.210
The fact is, over the past 20 years we have been interacting with technology in ever more intimate ways.

10
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:10.210
The Tamagotchi craze of the 1990s had people giving up their lives to take care of tiny digital pets.

11
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:15.210
In the early 2000s, Sony's robot dog, Ibo, stole people's hearts.

12
00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:20.210
And in 2011, Apple's Siri gave iPhones voices and personalities.

13
00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:25.210
Nowadays, we often spend more time with our phones than we do with other people.

14
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:31.210
Artificial intelligence will continue to simulate human personalities and behavior ever more accurately,

15
00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:38.210
and the barriers against falling in love with artificial humans may soon fall away altogether as a result.

16
00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:44.210
Indeed, surveys show that 30% of people feel they could fall in love with robots in the future.

17
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:50.210
One scientist even predicts that human-robot marriages will be legal by 2050.

18
00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.210
Technology is, of course, meant to make our lives easier.

19
00:01:54.210 --> 00:02:01.210
In this case, however, it seems the more advanced technology gets, the more complicated the situation might become.

20
00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:05.210
But then again, when was true love ever simple?
